---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import LakeFeature from '../../components/LakeFeature.astro';
import ConversationCTA from '../../components/ConversationCTA.astro';
import { lakes } from '../../data/lakes';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../utils/schema';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="A Closer Look at Rockford-Area Lake Living"
  description="Bostwick Lake, Silver Lake, Lake Bella Vista, Myers Lake and Brower Lake: a practical guide to buying or selling lake property in the Rockford area."
  path="/waterfront/rockford-lakes/"
  jsonLd={[
    breadcrumbSchema([
      { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { name: 'Waterfront', href: '/waterfront/' },
      { name: 'Rockford-area lakes' },
    ]),
  ]}
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Waterfront · Rockford"
    title="A closer look at Rockford-area lake living"
    lede="I’ve spent the last 15 years living on two Rockford-area lakes: seven years on Lake Bella Vista and the last eight on Silver Lake. I’ve also helped many clients buy and sell lakefront homes throughout the area. This is how I think about choosing a lake."
    breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Waterfront', href: '/waterfront/' }, { name: 'Rockford-area lakes' }]}
    tone="limestone"
  >
    <nav aria-label="Jump to a lake" class="jump">
      <ul>
        {lakes.map((l) => <li><a href={`#${l.slug}`}>{l.name}</a></li>)}
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container container--narrow prose">
      <h2>Every lake has its own personality.</h2>
      <p>
        Two lakes a few minutes apart can feel completely different, and so can two stretches of the same
        shoreline. The right choice depends on how you want to use the water, how you want the property to
        feel, and what you’re willing to take care of.
      </p>
      <p>
        The sections below are a starting point. I’m building this resource carefully and adding lake-specific
        details only as they’re confirmed, so I’d rather tell you what to ask than guess at what isn’t verified.
        I’m always glad to talk through a specific lake in person.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight" aria-label="The lakes">
    <div class="container">
      {lakes.map((l, i) => <LakeFeature lake={l} flip={i % 2 === 1} />)}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--lake" aria-labelledby="early-heading">
    <div class="container container--narrow stack">
      <span class="eyebrow">Staying prepared</span>
      <h2 id="early-heading">Waterfront homes can move quickly.</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="color:#e8eef0">
        Some opportunities begin through conversations long before a sign goes in the yard. After more than 15
        years working locally, and 15 years living on Rockford-area lakes myself, I often have context and
        relationships that help me stay close to what may be changing.
      </p>
      <p>
        I can’t promise a property before it reaches the market, but I can help you stay prepared when the
        right opportunity appears. A saved search is a good way to start.
      </p>
      <a class="btn btn--light" href="/home-search/?community=rockford">Send me Rockford-area lake homes</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="guide-heading">
    <div class="container container--narrow stack">
      <h2 id="guide-heading">Keep reading</h2>
      <p>
        My broader <a href="/waterfront/">waterfront guide</a> covers shoreline, access, docks, due diligence and
        resale across any lake. If you’re still deciding where to live, try <a href="/find-your-fit/">Find Your West
        Michigan Fit</a> or see my <a href="/communities/rockford/">Rockford community guide</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="small muted">
        This page offers general guidance only. It is not legal, environmental, or engineering advice, and it
        states no lake-specific rules, depths, acreage, frontage, access designations, or market statistics.
        Please confirm anything specific with the appropriate authority or a qualified professional.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ConversationCTA
    title="Have a lake in mind?"
    text="Tell me which one, or tell me what you want from the water, and I’ll help you narrow it down."
    label="Talk with me about lake living"
    href="/contact/?interest=waterfront"
  />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .jump ul {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-xs) var(--space-m);
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .jump li {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .jump a {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.4rem 0;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    color: var(--c-lake-deep);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-sand-deep);
  }
  .jump a:hover {
    border-color: var(--c-lake-deep);
  }
</style>
